{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be","id":994648,"title":"You as a Player Character: What Splat would you want to be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-28T10:05:32-07:00","id":994648,"title":"You as a Player Character: What Splat would you want to be?","content":"Yes, I shamelessly stole <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\">Aya Tari</a></b>'s Idea from here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/993767-what-beginning-creature-would-you-want-to-be\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...you-want-to-be</a><br /> If you could pick any of the Splats (- Mages) to become one of them (as a starting character) in our world, which one would you choose (and if you'd like to share, why?)<br /> You are welcome to state your favored skills and/or subsplats as well.<br /> <br /> E.g. Something like &quot;Vampire&quot;; &quot;Werewolf, because I like the tought of being able to turn into a wolf or killing-machine whenever I feel like it&quot; or &quot;Ferrum Tammuz with a lot of Corporeum&quot;<br /> <br /> NO MAGES, because I assume they'd be the top spot and chosen by the most, and I want diversity =P If you wouldn't have picked them anyway, I'd be much obliged if you left a statement to that effect (and maybe add why xD)<br /> <br /> Bonus: Assuming you'd be a character with (your Age-18) xp, which additional Skills/Merits/Abilities would you be having?<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd like to be a Beast, probably an Anakim or Makara Tyrant with Mimir's Wisdom/ Siren's Treacherous Song, Eye of Heaven, Unbreakable and Relentless, because I think that would allow me to live my life with relatively few changes while offering some additional sense of security and comfort.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: For clarification, the question is not &quot;Which Splat describes you best&quot; but &quot;Which splat would you <i>want </i>to be?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 03-08-2017, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:18:18-07:00","id":994652,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I did a thread like this as a poll and Mages blew everyone out of the water with about 43% of the votes (30 total). Werewolves came in a distant second with 8 votes or about 11%. I'll stand by the opinion I had then, though. If I had to be a CofD template, I'd go with Promethean for the hope of becoming human again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:01:34-07:00","id":994691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=994652#post994652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I did a thread like this as a poll and Mages blew everyone out of the water with about 43% of the votes (30 total). Werewolves came in a distant second with 8 votes or about 11%. I'll stand by the opinion I had then, though. If I had to be a CofD template, I'd go with Promethean for the hope of becoming human again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, Werewolves were second? I'd never have guessed that.<br /> <br /> That's unexpected, but I guess I understand your reasoning. I think managing to become a Redeemed would offer an additional benefit: you'd enjoy a very different outlook on life and subsequently a different degree of satisfaction, too. Still, I'd consider this a corageous choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:06:04-07:00","id":994696,"title":"","content":"Playing werewolf is awesome, and they don't have many disadvantages. It's not as weighted towards advantages as mages but Forsaken doesn't play the condition as a downer. And the bonuses are more appreciable to the general person. To quote the book, 'Being a werewolf is fucking awesome.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:14:17-07:00","id":994704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=994696#post994696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing werewolf is awesome, and they don't have many disadvantages. It's not as weighted towards advantages as mages but Forsaken doesn't play the condition as a downer. And the bonuses are more appreciable to the general person. To quote the book, 'Being a werewolf is fucking awesome.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I was kind of unimpressed by 1 ed. Have been repeatedly told 2ed is better. Guess I should give it a try^^<br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:24:30-07:00","id":994709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=994691#post994691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, Werewolves were second? I'd never have guessed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not too surprising to me, and I'd bet they'll come in first if you exclude Mages. They're pretty light on drawbacks, the biggest being Kuruth, and that can mostly be managed by keeping Harmony in check, maybe a couple of Rites for good measure. Personally though, I wouldn't be able to do it. It's a violent life style no matter what, and I don't know if I could stomach the urge to hunt, particularly not the prey they tend to favor. I can see the appeal, but it wouldn't be for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=994691#post994691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's unexpected, but I guess I understand your reasoning. I think managing to become a Redeemed would offer an additional benefit: you'd enjoy a very different outlook on life and subsequently a different degree of satisfaction, too. Still, I'd consider this a corageous choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an idealistic choice for sure, easier to make when it's purely hypothetical. I'd like to think I would stick by it if I actually had to make such a choice for real, but it's possible with the gravity of it staring me in the face I might well chicken out and go with something easier like a Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:26:54-07:00","id":994711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=994704#post994704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. I was kind of unimpressed by 1 ed. Have been repeatedly told 2ed is better. Guess I should give it a try^^<br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who really wanted to like Werewolf in 1e but always found it unsatisfying, 2e is <i>much</i> better. It pretty much fixed all of the problems I had with 1e and emphasized the parts that I liked most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:46:08-07:00","id":994719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=994711#post994711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who really wanted to like Werewolf in 1e but always found it unsatisfying, 2e is <i>much</i> better. It pretty much fixed all of the problems I had with 1e and emphasized the parts that I liked most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Sounds a lot like me re: 1ed. Now I am curious. Like, a lot. Guess I'll go pick up a pdf soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:17:06-07:00","id":994741,"title":"","content":"I can see why people pick werewolf, but I've never seen them as unbalancingly positive. I mean, keep in mind the gameplay is just abstractions. Kuruth is a mathematical way of representing the sheer, boiling RAGE that's always somewhere inside of you. I don't think I could handle that, combined with a constant urge to hunt and assert my own authority (I mean, come on, look at the pointless fights I've picked, and imagine how much worse that would have been if half my soul was literally made from conceptual embodiments of aggression and territoriality). And I would definitely strongly recommend 2e to anyone who had trouble getting into 1e. <br /> <br /> Let's see...can we do minor templates? Being a casual sorcerer or mad scientist wouldn't be that bad. Demon has sheer cool factor going for it, plus being able to switch bodies and having my true form be a monstrous chimeric aggregate of coalesced data would do wonders for my dysphoria, since True Form vs. Cover is pretty much already how I see myself online vs. in real life, but I'm going to try to keep from making this a ten paragraph gush about how much I love demon in so many ways, and why being a disabled trans communist is part of that. <br /> <br /> Promethean has some upsides too. Being an Unfleshed would also take care of my dysphoria, since a robot body would pretty much fix all my problems. <br /> <br /> I have to admit, the one I've actually given the most thought to is being a vampire, and that definitely has some appeal. I would 100% be Ordo Dracul, for the obvious reasons. I'm surprised Sin-Eaters didn't score higher, they're ridiculously overpowered and without many real downsides (hopefully second edition is going to do something about this). <br /> <br /> Demon, Changeling, and Beast all have an &quot;extradimensional personal pocket dimension&quot; option, which would be pretty neat. You know, I'm sure lots of people claim they'd want to be mages because they'd love to be enlightened and explore the cosmos and so on, but really the best reason to go with them is the sheer utility of magic. <br /> <br /> Also, I usually think of Mage as its own thing apart from the wider setting, and the original thread was kind of one of the things that made me start doing that. But for the record- Silver Ladder Obrimos or Mastigos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:16:09-07:00","id":994775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=994741#post994741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see why people pick werewolf, but I've never seen them as unbalancingly positive. I mean, keep in mind the gameplay is just abstractions. Kuruth is a mathematical way of representing the sheer, boiling RAGE that's always somewhere inside of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if this is off-topic, but I don't really think the whole constant state of rage thing is so much the case in Forsaken, at least not in 2e. Rage in this sense is more of an Apocalypse concept that got held over into 1e Forsaken and 2e has kind of moved away from. In my understanding, it's not so much that Uratha's rage is constantly simmering and Kuruth is it boiling over, more so that Werewolves are in part spirits of the hunt, and spirits cannot go against their nature. If you don't hunt willingly, your nature forces you to hunt unwillingly. Despite the name you're not <i>necessarily</i> angry when you Death Rage, you're just in a state where you are ruled by your spiritual instincts, and those instincts tell you to kill anything that looks like it might be prey. Kuruth Triggers aren't things that upset you, they're things that speak to your inner spirit and tell it now is the time to hunt. Your Auspice Moon brings out the wolf in you. The smell of blood makes you crave the kill. Your packmates being injured kicks your survival instincts into action. The sting of silver forces the spirit to defend itself. The presence of other supernatural creatures tempts you with exotic prey. It's not about rage, it's about predatory drive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-28-2016, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:25:47-07:00","id":994781,"title":"","content":"I mean, yeah, but given how angry people, myself included, can get over trivial things even without any of that, I still don't think it would be pleasant to have inside of you, even if they don't directly correlate to anger.<br /> <br /> As an even greater aside, though, that's an element I'll keep in mind if I ever design any other Shifters/Claimed, since I should have a &quot;The X Must Y&quot; statement for all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:37:03-07:00","id":994788,"title":"","content":"This is a hard choice. My first choice was disqualified, so ...<br /> <br /> I'd go for Mekhet, but I am torn on Covenant - Carthian, Circle, or Ordo Dracul. I'm not actually sure I'd want to be a vampire, given that being a vampire sucks in a lot of ways, but ESP takes the edge off. So does immortality. I'd miss my favorite foods, but that depends on whether blush of life makes food enjoyable again (although the need to vomit it back up remains).<br /> <br /> Maybe Eshmaki Nemesis, but I kind of think that would put me in a position of doing things I'd hate to do to survive. I basically picked the things that haunt me most when I have nightmares (or when I have disturbing dreams that are somehow not nightmares) to get this. I'd probably prefer family dinner over regular feeding, if I could find other supernaturals with whom I could hang out.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is Irraka Bone Shadow. I love shapeshifters and would love to be one myself. I picked Bone Shadow for reasons similar to picking Mekhet, and Irraka for similar reasons that I picked Eshmaki. Plus I am pretty stealthy and like it.<br /> <br /> 28 experiences is a lot to go on. I'd probably spend a lot of them on merits to guarantee a safe place, resources, and contacts. I'd spend the rest on supernatural powers and/or power traits. Definitely would buy Lair as a beast or Primal-Urge as a werewolf, not sure about Blood Potency. Would pick up more supernatural powers as well. This is all very vague but I don't have the books open in front of me. Would learn some athletics and another combat skill for self-defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-28-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:38:47-07:00","id":994791,"title":"","content":"Phenomenologist, from Genius the Transgression. Because who wouldn't want to be the sort of person where just talking to you is dangerous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:55:00-07:00","id":994807,"title":"","content":"Purified, with emphasis on Spiritual Defense Siddhi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:48:48-07:00","id":994860,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, ruling out Mages makes the selection tough. I wouldn't want to be urged to hurt people, that rules out Vampire and Beast. Being prone to mad breaks of fury ain't really my style, which knocks out Werewolf. Promethean is just suffering, no thanks. Mummies are slaves, no thanks. Changelings and Demons are constantly hiding and putting up facades, which is exhausting, but at least they have some agency to strike back. Maybe a Sin-Eater, they've still got it kinda good (though I'm expecting 2e to make their lives a tad darker). If minor splats are an option I'd probably go for of some sort Proximi, hopefully without an overly debilitating curse. <br /> <br /> But this is all pointless, the forums already decided I was a Demon. No point in arguing with the masses <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> \u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T16:32:07-07:00","id":994938,"title":"","content":"I'd be a Sin Eater, because <i>ghost buddy in my head</i>. Other than that, I'd have to stick to minor templates - body thieves would be on the top of the list.<br /> <br /> If I'm not restricted to <i>playable</i> splats - Idigam.<i> Definitely</i> Idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T18:57:56-07:00","id":994998,"title":"","content":"I'd probably go Demon. I'm one of the few people that are willing to go all in with immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:04:15-07:00","id":995002,"title":"","content":"Whichever one I wind up, I still probably kill myself on day one.<br /> <br /> These are <i>horror games</i>, people. Being any of these critters is fucking miserable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:13:25-07:00","id":995003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995002#post995002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whichever one I wind up, I still probably kill myself on day one.<br /> <br /> These are <i>horror games</i>, people. Being any of these critters is fucking miserable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are pretty awesome, don't front <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:22:29-07:00","id":995011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995002#post995002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whichever one I wind up, I still probably kill myself on day one.<br /> <br /> These are <i>horror games</i>, people. Being any of these critters is fucking miserable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still mystifies me that people call these horror games. All I'm going to say is that playing host to a creepy ghost pal sounds pretty appealing from where I'm standing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:32:07-07:00","id":995016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995011#post995011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still mystifies me that people call these horror games. All I'm going to say is that playing host to a creepy ghost pal sounds pretty appealing from where I'm standing.</div> </div> </div> </div>By all means, tell me how happy everyone with voices in their heads are in our world, and then take that but make the voices only talk about death. If something alien is sharing your body with you, <i>you have a parasite.</i><br /> <br /> How the hell are you not reading horror into any of these games when they explicitly tell you as much?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:41:50-07:00","id":995020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995016#post995016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By all means, tell me how happy everyone with voices in their heads are in our world, and then take that but make the voices only talk about death. If something alien is sharing your body with you, <i>you have a parasite.</i><br /> <br /> How the hell are you not reading horror into any of these games when they explicitly tell you as much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can honestly say that I'd be happier without the sinking, cavernously empty silence lodged where I <i>assume</i> other people have stuff like &quot;the capacity to love and/or feel anything other than a pale mockery of positive emotions&quot;. Please don't assume that &quot;happy&quot; actually means something to me, or that I fear death.<br /> <br /> I don't read horror into them because <i>they don't horrify me</i>. It doesn't matter <i>in the least</i> that other people think they should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:48:22-07:00","id":995022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995020#post995020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can honestly say that I'd be happier without the sinking, cavernously empty silence lodged where I <i>assume</i> other people have stuff like &amp;quot;the capacity to love and/or feel anything other than a pale mockery of positive emotions&amp;quot;. Please don't assume that &amp;quot;happy&amp;quot; actually means something to me, or that I fear death.<br /> <br /> I don't read horror into them because <i>they don't horrify me</i>. It doesn't matter <i>in the least</i> that other people think they should.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to disagree (and it sounds like you have plenty on your plate), but when the books, writers, and fans all call them horror games... well. <br /> <br /> A nihilist can understand what makes Lovecraft horror even if they see nothing horrific in a universe devoid of meaning or benevolent higher powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:03:52-07:00","id":995032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995002#post995002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whichever one I wind up, I still probably kill myself on day one.<br /> <br /> These are <i>horror games</i>, people. Being any of these critters is fucking miserable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The horror in the World of Darkness is reliant on the ST giving the story. Not to mention that just because being a supernatural doesn't mean you'll be consigned to misery, it's still possible to make something good/happy out of your life. The WoD isn't Warhammer.<br /> <br /> Although taking out Mages? I feel like my second choice would have to beeeee Vampire. It (mainly Masquerade rather than Requiem) has a special place in my heart and I don't think I'd mind the Vampire lifestyle. It would be interesting learning lore from possibly the oldest beings in existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:06:16-07:00","id":995033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995032#post995032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The horror in the World of Darkness is reliant on the ST giving the story. Not to mention that just because being a supernatural doesn't mean you'll be consigned to misery, it's still possible to make something good/happy out of your life. The WoD isn't Warhammer.<br /> <br /> Although taking out Mages? I feel like my second choice would have to beeeee Vampire. It (mainly Masquerade rather than Requiem) has a special place in my heart and I don't think I'd mind the Vampire lifestyle. It would be interesting learning lore from possibly the oldest beings in existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire is a game where no matter what else happens, you are a notmal person violently transformed into someone who has to hurt people to survive. Prometheans enter a world that hates and rejects them for the crime of existing. Changelings all went through absolute dehumanizing hell and return to find themselves replaced.<br /> <br /> The premise of each and every game is horror, no matter what any ST does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:25:52-07:00","id":995045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995033#post995033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire is a game where no matter what else happens, you are a notmal person violently transformed into someone who has to hurt people to survive. Prometheans enter a world that hates and rejects them for the crime of existing. Changelings all went through absolute dehumanizing hell and return to find themselves replaced.<br /> <br /> The premise of each and every game is horror, no matter what any ST does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not discussing the premise of the games. I'm discussing factor of living as one. It's possible for Vampires to feed without killing people (or even traumatizing them) and maintain humanity. Prometheans can live nomadically and eventually become human. Changelings can return to their old lives (either by melding with the Fetch or killing it and replacing it) and try to keep living in their old lives, keeping their heads down from the True Fae. Even though the premise is horror, it doesn't mean that work can't be done to minimize that in their lives.<br /> <br /> I'll also rephrase, while there is horror in the World of Darkness, it's the ST who decides how prevalent that premise is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:44:27-07:00","id":995049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995045#post995045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not discussing the premise of the games. I'm discussing factor of living as one. It's possible for Vampires to feed without killing people (or even traumatizing them) and maintain humanity. Prometheans can live nomadically and eventually become human. Changelings can return to their old lives (either by melding with the Fetch or killing it and replacing it) and try to keep living in their old lives, keeping their heads down from the True Fae. Even though the premise is horror, it doesn't mean that work can't be done to minimize that in their lives.<br /> <br /> I'll also rephrase, while there is horror in the World of Darkness, it's the ST who decides how prevalent that premise is.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic, the Chronicles of Darkness setting is all about gnome because any Storyteller can add lots of them to a given chronicle.<br /> <br /> A Vampire that only feeds on animals or tries to feed humanely is doing so knowing that they spend every night of the rest of eternity one Frenzy away from killing someone; they're acting the way they are because monstrosity is constantly gnawing at their heels. A chronicle with a protagonist like that is explicitly horror because they're basing their actions around a likely moral spiral of frightening closeness, and that's decidedly horror.<br /> <br /> Also, trying to live your old life after returning from an absolute nightmare is definitely horror, as is the constant paranoia that maybe the Fae will notice you again and drag you away from your flimsy little life. Your rebuke speaks to my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:59:01-07:00","id":995056,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'd mind being a Sin Eater, going purely by the little I know of them. Assuming I'm extremely off basis as to the average day to day dealings of a Sin Eater and that it much worse than I think I'd then go with Changeling. Changelings have a bit of baggage, but nothing I don't think I'd be unable to deal with. Demons come in third. I love just about everything about them, but they're so <i>annoyingly secretive</i>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T22:20:32-07:00","id":995079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995049#post995049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By that logic, the Chronicles of Darkness setting is all about gnome because any Storyteller can add lots of them to a given chronicle.<br /> <br /> A Vampire that only feeds on animals or tries to feed humanely is doing so knowing that they spend every night of the rest of eternity one Frenzy away from killing someone; they're acting the way they are because monstrosity is constantly gnawing at their heels. A chronicle with a protagonist like that is explicitly horror because they're basing their actions around a likely moral spiral of frightening closeness, and that's decidedly horror.<br /> <br /> Also, trying to live your old life after returning from an absolute nightmare is definitely horror, as is the constant paranoia that maybe the Fae will notice you again and drag you away from your flimsy little life. Your rebuke speaks to my point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well you're right about horror being involved, and I can assure you that I can see what some of the horror in these games. But from what I can tell, Chronicles of Darkness also has a prevailing sense of Hope. Yes, Changelings had an absolutely awful experience, but they've gotten out and they'll band together to prevent ever going back; hell, some even fight back against those who oppressed them. While it is true that Vampires have to feed upon the living to survive, but from what I can tell part of Vampire's theme is about accepting that part of your life because you can't change it; the hope comes from being able to minimize that damage and finding a purpose in your new life (via the Covenants). As for Sin-Eaters, if memory serves part of their whole premise was celebrating life and how precious it is. I do understand where you're coming from, and if this was Classic World of Darkness then I'd be behind you one hundred percent; but I've always felt that Chronicles of Darkness has always had a bit more hope to it than it's predecessor did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T22:22:06-07:00","id":995081,"title":"","content":"Oh, and in the original vein of the topic I think I'd like to be a Mekhet or a Nosferatu, and if I had to pick a covenant it'd probably be the Ordo Dracul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T22:25:32-07:00","id":995082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995033#post995033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampire is a game where no matter what else happens, you are a notmal person violently transformed into someone who has to hurt people to survive. Prometheans enter a world that hates and rejects them for the crime of existing. Changelings all went through absolute dehumanizing hell and return to find themselves replaced.<br /> <br /> The premise of each and every game is horror, no matter what any ST does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, all three of those are definitively horror games where horrible things happen to change you.<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Mage aren't, though. Like, bad things can happen to you, yes, and werewolves can have a very bad First Change experience, but they don't <i>need</i> to.<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Mage are definitively games about becoming something empowering, something more than what you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T22:39:04-07:00","id":995084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995079#post995079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you're right about horror being involved, and I can assure you that I can see what some of the horror in these games. But from what I can tell, Chronicles of Darkness also has a prevailing sense of Hope. Yes, Changelings had an absolutely awful experience, but they've gotten out and they'll band together to prevent ever going back; hell, some even fight back against those who oppressed them. While it is true that Vampires have to feed upon the living to survive, but from what I can tell part of Vampire's theme is about accepting that part of your life because you can't change it; the hope comes from being able to minimize that damage and finding a purpose in your new life (via the Covenants). As for Sin-Eaters, if memory serves part of their whole premise was celebrating life and how precious it is. I do understand where you're coming from, and if this was Classic World of Darkness then I'd be behind you one hundred percent; but I've always felt that Chronicles of Darkness has always had a bit more hope to it than it's predecessor did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hope is necessary to make the horror more terrible by contrast, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T23:19:41-07:00","id":995093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995084#post995084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hope is necessary to make the horror more terrible by contrast, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with that sentiment. If a game didn't have any sense of hope then the horror would just start feeling a little bland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":". 10-29-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T00:42:12-07:00","id":995105,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> So basically I took the question as &quot;You have to be <i>something</i> in the CofD, which would you choose? Mages are right out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course being one of these creature types sucks in many ways and being one wouldn't be all that great, but that doesn't mean there's anything wrong with answering the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T01:22:59-07:00","id":995118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995105#post995105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> So basically I took the question as &quot;You have to be <i>something</i> in the CofD, which would you choose? Mages are right out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course being one of these creature types sucks in many ways and being one wouldn't be all that great, but that doesn't mean there's anything wrong with answering the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>That fits very well, thanks. English isn't my first language, so sometimes I get stuck on a different train of thought and express myself a bit ambigious.<br /> <br /> What I also find striking is that most people (including me) go for &quot;what would upset my life the least?&quot; It's interesting that a lot of people went for minor splats, hadn't really considered that at all, but good thinking, especially in when keeping my former statement in mind.<br /> <br /> However, I still think that, if you're willing to pay the prize, their lifes CAN be worthwile/satisfying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T04:53:29-07:00","id":995153,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm. I think either a Werewolf (Rahu, Cahalith or Irraka) or a Vampire (Gangrel, Ventrue or Nosferatu). Vampire has the appeal of potential everlasting existence but with the possibility of just being dead for long periods of time (via Torpor). Werewolf is all about purity and power I must admit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T05:01:29-07:00","id":995156,"title":"","content":"I'd probably go with Beast. Some sort of Nemesis, because shit, let's be Batman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T08:03:01-07:00","id":995199,"title":"","content":"What would I <i>want</i> to be? Well that's a really difficult question, because now I have you pick favorites and you removed mages so I can't use magic to become an abominable lich and enjoy the world as long as I want before I escape it through Ascension.<br /> <br /> But only 8xp to go on kinda sucks... I think I'll go with a werewolf. Lots of neat innate stat bonuses and goodies, and I live in a rural area anyway so I can get a lot of mileage out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:46:23-07:00","id":995283,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't want to be any of them, but if I had to be one, Beast, Ugallu Nemesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:07:04-07:00","id":995289,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Some of the powers Changeling have are so appealing to me that i might want to go into a durance to get them :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:11:42-07:00","id":995294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995283#post995283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't want to be any of them, but if I had to be one, Beast, Ugallu Nemesis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you have wings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:23:28-07:00","id":995298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995294#post995294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you have wings?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The angels that fell from heaven didn't need wings to fly.&quot;<br /> <br /> But honestly, could go either way. I would fly either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:31:46-07:00","id":995301,"title":"","content":"Werewolf, again. Especially with second edition, the powers and gifts drastically outweigh the downsides, which to me would be up sides for the most part. Sacred Hunt hooooooo.<br /> <br /> Query. Idle, not a serious sticking point. These surveys pop up a lot, and I always get tangled when the questioner specifies, 'in our world.' Our world, as far as I'm aware, lacks a Shadow, Supernal forces, strix, and so on. While in some cases, like this strix or True Fae, their lack acts as a benefit to the supernatural, in others like mages and werewolves it's a huge disadvantage, as they lack access to a lot of powers. For the most part I figure I'm reading too much into it, because I'm increasingly tired and stressed and seek clarity in posts that is often assumed or simply not offered by the poster. But, basically, how much of the supernatural's baggage comes with them? Does a vampire have to deal with elders? Does a werewolf have access to the Hisil? Will a mage provoke Paradox? And so forth.<br /> <br /> I would never be able to look at a rat or spider again the way I do now, if azlu and beshilu were real. Imagine if any spider could contain the shard of a lost ancient horror that might crawl inside a loved one, or yourself, or a complete stranger down the street and start a body horror version of Sinister Spider-man in an attempt to resurrect its forebear, which if successful would probably wreak a streak of Godzilla-like havoc across the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-29-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T12:49:31-07:00","id":995304,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the derail, but... need to say this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995032#post995032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The horror in the World of Darkness is reliant on the ST giving the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to disagree <i>strongly</i> with this statement. There's a degree to which, yeah, everything in a TTRPG relies on the ST facilitating things by cultivating this, putting that off limits, challenging you with this, pulling you with that.<br /> <br /> But there are two kinds of horror, in my view: externally-generated, and internally-generated. The ST can only provide externally-generated horror: scary boojums that leap out of the shadows with lolling tongues and susurrations whispering you into insanity. Sure, and that's great. I tend to find that kind of horror bland, personally, so I don't give it a lot of thought. What I find interesting, and what I think that CofD as a whole does exceptionally well, is internally-generated horror.<br /> <br /> Instead of describing that right now, let me paste something I wrote a while back:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Other Poster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way my group plays WoD is much closer to Urban Fantasy with supernatural societies, clashing personalities and territorial politics and power plays than slice of life and/or horror and I'm wondering how you've changed things to suit what you prefer.<br /> <br /> In fact...I'm almost not sure what horror gameplay even entails. Can someone share what goes on in a regular session that they consider to be a horror themed game?</div> </div> </div> </div>For me? It's having enough carrots that your player is willing to do something terrible, and then having enough self-reflection that they can look back, from an OOC perspective, and find their character's actions repulsive. The subjective-stat mechanic is just a way, IMO, to <i>prompt</i> that self-reflection.<br /> <br /> Of course, the thing about horror is that it's supposed to leave you unsettled. That's part of the definition. So horror generally doesn't get placed at the end of things: it gets placed in the preparation and the lead-up, at most, and then the PCs go and clean everything up and make everything better and feel very good about themselves.<br /> <br /> But really where horror belongs, in an RPG? Is as a constant, inexorable temptation. You should constantly be finding reasons to do something terrible. It should be obvious, convenient, easy. You should be staring down the barrel of the gun, knowing all the time that it'd be simpler to just pull that trigger and kill that fucker. Let the Paradox go. Let Kuruth consume you. Let yourself Embrace him. Let yourself betray your motleymate. Choose to let go of humanity, just this once. It would solve the problem. It would solve it quickly, and efficiently, and damn the consequences. Move fast. Break things. That's what a PC does, right?<br /> <br /> That kind of horror can work at the session-level, I think, because all you have to do is find situations where there's a meaningful choice between something horrific but easy and something boring but difficult. And as a player, you get tired of doing the hard thing. Or you're bored of doing the right thing. So you take a dramatic failure. Or you choose to do the wrong thing. And you roll that subjective stat. You ask if it's worth it. Of course it is. You're bored; you're frustrated; you're willing to break a few eggs because this omelette needs to just be <i>done</i>.<br /> <br /> Suggestion: have your players write a diary entry about every roll they make against their subjective stat. Three or four sentences is enough; it's not supposed to be an essay. But have them really get inside their character's head, and figure out what that roll meant, internally, introspectively. Piece those entries together after the chronicle. Talk about them together. Talk about what your characters did, whether it was the right thing to do, if it was worth it.<br /> <br /> See if that helps you find the horror. Or, at least, see if it helps you find the self-justification.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, the ST's job is much less about &quot;how to horrify your players&quot; and more &quot;how to set up situations in which the players horrify themselves&quot;. And I think that that's an important distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:14:39-07:00","id":995312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995002#post995002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are <i>horror games</i>, people. Being any of these critters is fucking miserable.</div> </div> </div> </div> And being human isn't? Everything is miserable if you look at it the right way. Being human in the CofD doesn't give you a pass on the horror or misery.<br /> <br /> I personally come from the standpoint that all the playable supernaturals, save Prometheans and Demons, should still be considered human. I personally find the default CofD view on what classifies as &quot;human&quot; to be restrictive and overly regid. These games are written to reflect parts of the human condition, which makes each of these so-called monsters part of humanity and our lives. I personally can't separate the two of them. Plus, if you use the &quot;can have children&quot; line for species, then most supernaturals are still considered <i>homo sapien.</i> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995082#post995082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf and Mage aren't, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure they are. &quot;A game of Savage Horror&quot; is Werewolf's tagline. And mage is supposed to be about the horror of power / hubris / etc. People might not <i>play</i> the games like horror, but its definitely meant to be there. <br /> <br /> Frankly, I think that werewof is terrifying to be part of. You're basically in an eternal war against spirits, racists wolves, and any number of things that want eat you. I'm honestly surprised every werewolf over a year doesn't suffer from some variation of PTSD. Werewolf's basic setting is sheer hell. As for Mage? Yeah, I was never sold on the premises of its horror simply because I disagree with it and its presentation. Still intended on being a horror game, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:28:06-07:00","id":995319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995312#post995312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I think that werewof is terrifying to be part of. You're basically in an eternal war against spirits, racists wolves, and any number of things that want eat you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, werewolves encounter some really nasty stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm honestly surprised every werewolf over a year doesn't suffer from some variation of PTSD. Werewolf's basic setting is sheer hell. </div> </div> </div>I think it's a personal thing, but also that the werewolf's new psychology and environment factors into it. Their human mind is remade to that of a werewolf, a being of change that can and is in fact designed to deal with things like this. Some who went through particularly harrowing experiences, or lean more towards their 'human brain' might fall to it more often but most werewolves would have their mind built in a way that such things don't linger in an ill fashion. Also you have an entire society basically offering support and tacit approval of what needs to be done. The Wolf Must Hunt. Not The Wolf Must Hunt And You're Bad Because Of It. Brands of Renown for Cunning, Glory, Honor, Purity, and Wisdom, appreciating that there is more to the hunt and life than just bloodshed.<br /> <br /> I'd be surprised if Stew or someone wasn't basing at least some of the ideas on the studies on the military and other conflict-driven lives. Studies done by Dave Grossman and SLA Marshall have shown the reasons for PTSD, reluctance to kill and other issues that come up on the battlefield and off. And werewolf has neat ways to deal with the issues. With the Oath of the Moon and the compelling reason to need the hunt, one has a moral reason to go about it and face the things werewolves face. With the pack, they are not alone and have a close group that can, ideally, support them when needed. And since the sacred hunt isn't something that, at least at first, needs to be frequently done, it's not as constantly draining on a newly-changed person the way a vampire having to drink blood might be. By the time you are hunting frequently, it's implied that your high Primal Urge has shifted you to become farther from that ordinary human you used to be. And while it's a daunting proposition, and should be, it also offers more capabilities to deal with what you need to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-29-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:31:36-07:00","id":995320,"title":"","content":"That's part of the horror really. Being a werewolf should be a traumatic experience, but it just... doesn't bother them, because they're fundamentally inhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:13:08-07:00","id":995343,"title":"","content":"I mean, MCN raises a good point in that I'd rather be any of them than human, in ChroD or in real life. Even a Promethean or a Changeling, honestly, seems better than being human to me. Access to immortality is a big part of it. Even the splats that aren't immortal are in a better position to achieve it than humans. Changelings can buy all the years they want if they spend enough time at the Goblin Market. Sin-Eaters know enough about death that one of them really shot for immortality they'd probably make it. And yet I'm still firmly with atamajakki in the &quot;these are horror games&quot; boat.<br /> <br /> Probably Demon, not just because of the powers but because when I read Demon for the first time, it spoke to me on some of the deepest levels anything has ever reached inside me. Demon has sort of been the anti-promethean in my life, because demon made me feel less alone. It made me feel like people understood, that I might be stuck in a world that wasn't made for people like me, but there were still stories for me, still things perfectly made for me to tell my story. I'm getting into a gush rant, which I said I wouldn't, but fuck it. I'd be a Demon because Demon meant so much to me. &quot;Don't let the world tell you that you're broken. You don't need to be fixed.&quot; I love Changeling, and a lot of people have made similarly deep connections with it, but Demon just connected with me in a way no other tabletop roleplaying game ever has. I love the hell out of Edge of the Empire and Eberron and so on, but Demon is literally my life. I've given other games shit for trying to capture the experiences of marginalized people and fumbling it, but Demon is proof that a game can get it so perfectly right. I have a Cover. The cover mechanic pretty much describes exactly what my life is like. My Cover is the me people see in the real world, the physical body I'm trapped in, the persona I put on to deal with people who can't know the real me, because I live in a dark, uncaring, twisted world where it seems like nature itself is against me. So that's why I'd go with Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-29-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:29:46-07:00","id":995350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995343#post995343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, MCN raises a good point in that I'd rather be any of them than human, in ChroD or in real life. Even a Promethean or a Changeling, honestly, seems better than being human to me. Access to immortality is a big part of it. Even the splats that aren't immortal are in a better position to achieve it than humans. Changelings can buy all the years they want if they spend enough time at the Goblin Market. Sin-Eaters know enough about death that one of them really shot for immortality they'd probably make it. And yet I'm still firmly with atamajakki in the &quot;these are horror games&quot; boat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Immortality in ChroD isn't exactly a free ride though. If age can't kill you then you end up waiting for something else to get you, and in ChroD that something else can make death seem a welcome alternative. For Changelings that could mean getting reclaimed by the Fae and dragged back into Arcadia, a full on fate worse than death. Prometheans have either a lynch mob or descent into flux to look forward to. Demons <i>might </i>be able to carve out a personal 'Hell' and live free from the God-Machine, but more likely they will have to live Cover to Cover, hiding for hundreds or even thousands of years till the machine finds them. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:31:01-07:00","id":995351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995350#post995350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immortality in ChroD isn't exactly a free ride though. If age can't kill you then you end up waiting for something else to get you, and in ChroD that something else can make death seem a welcome alternative. For Changelings that could mean getting reclaimed by the Fae and dragged back into Arcadia, a full on fate worse than death. Prometheans have either a lynch mob or descent into flux to look forward to. Demons <i>might </i>be able to carve out a personal 'Hell' and live free from the God-Machine, but more likely they will have to live Cover to Cover, hiding for hundreds or even thousands of years till the machine finds them. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Still better than dying, at least for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:33:15-07:00","id":995353,"title":"","content":"maybe I missed it, but nobody voted for Mummy.<br /> <br /> truly immortal, nigh unkillable, godly cosmic power, the faith and worship of an entire cult.<br /> The detail that appeals to me the most is Mummies have purpose; your gods are real, your works matter.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:35:25-07:00","id":995354,"title":"","content":"Pros: Your gods are real.<br /> <br /> Cons: Your gods are real assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:36:17-07:00","id":995356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995353#post995353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">maybe I missed it, but nobody voted for Mummy.<br /> <br /> truly immortal, nigh unkillable, godly cosmic power, the faith and worship of an entire cult.<br /> The detail that appeals to me the most is Mummies have purpose; your gods are real, your works matter.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the Sekhem cycle and loss of memories sucks pretty hard. Plus, you're as much a servant of your cult as they are yours. <br /> <br /> And your gods might exist, but they're kind of massive dicks, and it's kind of a major theme in the line that pursuing great works and lost glory will leave you with nothing, and the only real achievement mummies can work towards is recovering the truth about their origins and lives and freeing themselves from their condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T16:32:54-07:00","id":995424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995356#post995356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the only real achievement mummies can work towards is recovering the truth about their origins and lives and freeing themselves from their condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like Promethean, sans the hope!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T17:15:09-07:00","id":995439,"title":"","content":"Nah, there's hope, since it's still possible. Also, you get to keep the immortality. I guess the reason to pick Mummy is that their &quot;higher state&quot;, Apotheosis, is SPOILER one of the better forms of immortality you can get in ChroD. You still have some pretty neat powers, plus you have all those juicy memories back. <br /> <br /> If you're asking why I like Mummy and not 1e or 2e Promethean, I'm sticking to my resolution not to argue about that any more. Okay, one thing: I like that Apotheosis is an incredibly rare and possibly apocryphal event in Mummy, and that pursuing it runs against every impulse that's been baked into you. But I accept that that's just opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-29-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T19:54:11-07:00","id":995483,"title":"","content":"I identify best with Changeling, but I wouldn't want to be a changeling....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T20:13:15-07:00","id":995486,"title":"","content":"I'd like to be Purified.<br /> <br /> Sure, my powers aren't too great, and I'd probably have to swear fealty to some alien lord of Spirits.<br /> <br /> But I'd get to be immortal in a way that's genuinely, actually without any inherent downsides, and I get some small-scale supernatural powers such as &quot;sway people to my side&quot; or &quot;see really fucking far&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think that's pretty awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T20:36:11-07:00","id":995490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995439#post995439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, there's hope, since it's still possible. Also, you get to keep the immortality. I guess the reason to pick Mummy is that their &amp;quot;higher state&amp;quot;, Apotheosis, is SPOILER one of the better forms of immortality you can get in ChroD. You still have some pretty neat powers, plus you have all those juicy memories back. <br /> <br /> If you're asking why I like Mummy and not 1e or 2e Promethean, I'm sticking to my resolution not to argue about that any more. Okay, one thing: I like that Apotheosis is an incredibly rare and possibly apocryphal event in Mummy, and that pursuing it runs against every impulse that's been baked into you. But I accept that that's just opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I wasn't trying to ask about that, I was just making a joke <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T20:37:24-07:00","id":995491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995486#post995486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to be Purified.<br /> <br /> Sure, my powers aren't too great, and I'd probably have to swear fealty to some alien lord of Spirits.<br /> <br /> But I'd get to be immortal in a way that's genuinely, actually without any inherent downsides, and I get some small-scale supernatural powers such as &quot;sway people to my side&quot; or &quot;see really fucking far&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think that's pretty awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's why it is always my answer in those kinds of threads- the only biggest downside is that in order to become one you need to actually die and has a big chance you'll stay that way, but if you have been promised with 100% success, the only thing you have to worry about are the big and scary masters of the Shadow, and they are actually something everyone should be worried about (and Storm Lords who think you are some form of Claimed, but it is another thing everyone should be worried about).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T21:11:37-07:00","id":995495,"title":"","content":"Werewolf for me! I always liked werewolves and I could really see myself living that life. Having the ability to shapeshift, heal, have cool powers, have amazing health, and feel like you can do anything is awesome. Though having to constantly deal with rage can be really scary, especially to the ones you love. But hey, most of us deal with stress and anxiety all the time. As for having to deal with all the weird and dangerous spirits can be tough but fortunately werewolves have tons of resources to deal with them. And best of all you are never alone because you have a pack to support you. I think I would be Irraka or Rahu and bone shadows or hunters in darkness. So yeah, werewolf for me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2360,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","user":"Cecoyotl","date":". 10-30-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T22:37:24-07:00","id":995518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995490#post995490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, I wasn't trying to ask about that, I was just making a joke <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, sorry. Shouldn't have assumed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:35:40-07:00","id":995751,"title":"","content":"Really liking the discussion that sprang up here =D Didn't expect that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995301#post995301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Query. Idle, not a serious sticking point. These surveys pop up a lot, and I always get tangled when the questioner specifies, 'in our world.' Our world, as far as I'm aware, lacks a Shadow, Supernal forces, strix, and so on. While in some cases, like this strix or True Fae, their lack acts as a benefit to the supernatural, in others like mages and werewolves it's a huge disadvantage, as they lack access to a lot of powers. For the most part I figure I'm reading too much into it, because I'm increasingly tired and stressed and seek clarity in posts that is often assumed or simply not offered by the poster. But, basically, how much of the supernatural's baggage comes with them? Does a vampire have to deal with elders? Does a werewolf have access to the Hisil? Will a mage provoke Paradox? And so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, originally I meant it exactly like you mentioned &quot;in our world&quot;, with the addendum of things necessary for your setting to work to exist e.g. spirits/hisil are a thing, Elders not necessarily though, which would make the whole point of some covenants moot, however. Which is why I took the easy way out, assuming a complete shift to the world of CofD (as in, you actually life in it and simply don't know it yet).<br /> Anything else would, imo, require a hack and change too many variables (e.g. you as the only vampire there is would be something very different from being part of a kindred society. You as the only werewolf would turn it a lot more horrifying, whereas a &quot;magical change&quot; into a Changeling without a durance or the threat of the Fae or any of the downside to your personal life would make them a first-rate pick)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T13:48:01-07:00","id":995792,"title":"","content":"Oh! Yeah, if it's our world plus changes necessary for the template to work, I might actually go Sin-Eater instead of Promethean. Real-life ghost activity (assuming it's real, since that is one of those &quot;necessary to work&quot; things for Geist) seems less ubiquitous and more subdued than in ChroD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T14:56:07-07:00","id":995816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995353#post995353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">maybe I missed it, but nobody voted for Mummy.<br /> <br /> truly immortal, nigh unkillable, godly cosmic power, the faith and worship of an entire cult.<br /> The detail that appeals to me the most is Mummies have purpose; your gods are real, your works matter.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Extremely limited up-time and spend most of the job either being dragged around by a cult or going after memories and by the time that works out, it's time to sleep again.<br /> <br /> From the &quot;a Day in the life of&quot; Vampire is a more viable option.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm leaning Sin-Eaters mostly because it sounds like they're having a blast of a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T22:35:31-08:00","id":1004255,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'd absolutely be a Mysterium Ob... Dammit. &lt;sigh&gt;<br /> <br /> Sin-Eater, most likely. Probably Bonepicker, Advocate, or Necromancer. Threshold would likely be Silent or Forgotten.<br /> <br /> Normally I like shapeshifters, but Forsaken don't appeal to me. An Ithaeur is tempting though. I just don't know enough about the Tribes to settle on one. If the otherwise horrible Changing Breeds options are available, Bastet all the way. I love the fae, but the baggage that comes with being a Changeling is... yeah. OTOH, it would explain certain things in my life. So, maybe?<br /> <br /> Purified or Wardens might be cool. I'd also be willing to be a Lucifuge Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","name":"Ariketh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T04:30:14-08:00","id":1004332,"title":"","content":"I would be a Beast, dat Skeleton Key ability <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> would let me travel everywhere. <br /> Eshmaki most likely, though Makara and Anakim aren't bad either. <br /> <br /> The second choice would be a werecreature, just not a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T20:19:29-08:00","id":1004779,"title":"","content":"If I were to choose what's closest to my personality, I'd say Demon/Wheel/Tempter. I keep things running and I try to build my little pocket of happiness away from God. Ha, I can't really escape the cycles I'm bound to. I'd be a <span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Tef</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Aabhi Arisen. </span></span><br /> <br /> If I had to choose my fate, it would be Gangrel/Ordo Dracul. Strip away all the obfuscating ways humans feed on life and be honest about what we are. Plus, turning into a cloud of bats sounds fun. Go explore the supernatural and call it all Dragon's Nests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T09:01:30-08:00","id":1004974,"title":"","content":"Hmm. In terms of what I would <i>want</i> to be, I'm gonna have to say an Uratha. Preferably Elodoth, they seem the most balanced (while I usually play a Rahu, I don't need that sort of combat ability in real life). Tribe-wise I'd either be an Iron Master or a Hunter in Darkness: Iron Master if the assumption is that I'm the only werewolf and the world is otherwise the same, HiD if the attendant mythology comes with being a werewolf because I'm going to make sure nobody I love ever gets Shartha'd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T13:25:30-08:00","id":1005081,"title":"","content":"Iron Master Cahalith, since I love to write stories and love the idea of using hunting jerks and bad people in the community around me and then writing about that.<br /> <br /> My mentor figure/ parental substitute/editor of my book would probably be my TFV handler (My head canon is that TFV routinely uses supernaturals the way the FIB and IAA in GTA use criminals) in this take on me, since he used to be a navy intelligence officer (he once implied that he knew the truth behind MKULTRA but couldn't tell me because it would violate his security clearance)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T01:37:10-08:00","id":1007097,"title":"","content":"Probably Beast, but maybe Werewolf. Beast, because I think Lairs are one of the coolest things ever and I like the idea of exploring the supernatural which Beasts do a lot of. As for type, probably an Eshmaki with a Hunger for Punishment.<br /> <br /> While Werewolves have to deal with some pretty terrible things, they know what their purpose in life is and have some pretty cool powers. Not really sure on Auspice, but probably Rahu or Elodoth. I'd want to join the Storm Lords because I find their ethos appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T10:01:54-08:00","id":1007298,"title":"","content":"Tempted with werewolf... But I'd be worried about causing real harm if I got out of control in the wrong place. Plus, I don't know if any other werewolves and being a lone wolf loses some appeal. If there are others... I've gotta hope they're not jerks. Too violent for me as well. Still.... Tempting. <br /> <br /> If I had to embrace a supernatural type, warts and all, I'd go with a Beast. There's the requirement to feast, but I have some control as to who I target and to what extent I go to, so how much damage I cause can be mitigated with consideration. Losing control of the Horror for a night means that someone has a pretty bad nightmare, potentially, but I think that's preferable to ripping out throats. And that really gets to why I think it might be the better choice for me. I can rationalize a bit of awfulness.<br /> <br /> Beasts have some appealing advantages, though. Exploring the supernatural world is second nature to them. The Lair can be so evocative. And even if you come across something horrific... It's not really something that will likely shock you. Plus, Beasts have quite a bit of personal power. Eye of Heaven, Mimir's Wisdom and Needs Must are Atavisms that are great for advancing yourself. <br /> <br /> If I had to be a monster, I think I would prefer being a monster that's okay with being a monster. Maybe I could be an ethical monster? Be able to direct my predation onto targets that I'm sure are &quot;deserving&quot;? Maybe... Maybe not. There would probably come a time where I took things too far, and I would probably lie to myself that it was bound to happen, that monsters do monstrous things and that I can control myself so that I'm a better monster. <br /> <br /> In the end, though, I'd still be a monster. Maybe I could live with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T12:57:46-08:00","id":1007387,"title":"","content":"Assuming that non-mage doesn't include sub-splats i'd probably pick silver ladder proximi. Otherwise i'd go follower role construct promethean, rabbit or wolf headed changeling, or a geist that died of exhaustion trying to get home from the woods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T20:10:40-08:00","id":1007918,"title":"","content":"A demon from demon the decent and second would be a mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:12:48-08:00","id":1008373,"title":"","content":"Based on how my life seems to go, I would assume I am a Promethean .. but if I had my choice? perhaps a Beast.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T19:04:00-08:00","id":1009125,"title":"","content":"Ah... Could I be a Princess? Wouldn't necessary be a fan of being called a Princess all the time and would hope that my supernatural clique would come up a gender neutral name, but the Magical Girl superpowers and sweet outfits do appeal to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bBeing a batshit Genius wouldn't be so bad either so as long as I get cool looking goggles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T00:24:42-08:00","id":1009221,"title":"","content":"<b>Scion</b> or <b>Demon: the Fallen.</b> <b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 11-28-2016, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:29:27-08:00","id":1010495,"title":"","content":"Lucifuge. Live hundreds of years, get cool powers, fight the good fight, don't have to be an asshole to the undeserving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T22:25:41-08:00","id":1010521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=995816#post995816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Extremely limited up-time and spend most of the job either being dragged around by a cult or going after memories and by the time that works out, it's time to sleep again.<br /> <br /> From the &quot;a Day in the life of&quot; Vampire is a more viable option.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm leaning Sin-Eaters mostly because it sounds like they're having a blast of a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, my inclination is Mummy as well. For, like Promethean, it's one of the game lines with a clear element of hope. The immortality, immense power, and the chance to witness all of history are all well and good, if rather drowned out by the various downsides in my view, but there's the dream of Apotheosis lurking on the edges. The prospect of freedom.<br /> <br /> So Mummy is where I'm at, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:45:08-08:00","id":1011568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WaywardPaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1010495#post1010495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucifuge. Live hundreds of years, get cool powers, fight the good fight, don't have to be an asshole to the undeserving.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't the powers all hurt to use, though? I know that's the case with VASCU, which is why I'm wary of choosing that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T22:09:53-08:00","id":1013003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1011568#post1011568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't the powers all hurt to use, though? I know that's the case with VASCU, which is why I'm wary of choosing that</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all. Turning into a demon that causes Lunacy in supernaturals does hurt your body, though not much. The fire throwing ones lets you do more severe damage if you hurt yourself.<br /> <br /> Self harm is usually only if you choose the &quot;burn brighter&quot; option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:37:47-08:00","id":1013189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WaywardPaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1013003#post1013003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not all. Turning into a demon that causes Lunacy in supernaturals does hurt your body, though not much. The fire throwing ones lets you do more severe damage if you hurt yourself.<br /> <br /> Self harm is usually only if you choose the &quot;burn brighter&quot; option.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, that might be the best one then. Still not my pick since I'm Jewish","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:33:58-08:00","id":1013325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1013189#post1013189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, that might be the best one then. Still not my pick since I'm Jewish</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Curious how being Jewish would influence that? Assuming you'd be in the WoD of course and the cosmology is consistent. I don't subscribe to any notion of the supernatural beyond there being insufficient evidence to convince me, and had grown up in an Evangelical household. If I was in the Chronicles of Darkness, I'd seriously need to reassess that position :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:06:59-08:00","id":1013346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WaywardPaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1013325#post1013325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Curious how being Jewish would influence that? Assuming you'd be in the WoD of course and the cosmology is consistent. I don't subscribe to any notion of the supernatural beyond there being insufficient evidence to convince me, and had grown up in an Evangelical household. If I was in the Chronicles of Darkness, I'd seriously need to reassess that position :P</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cause the Lucifuge is a very Catholic organization. Or at least Christian","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:07:30-08:00","id":1013348,"title":"","content":"And this is a question of choice, and I don't want to have to change my religion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:23:50-08:00","id":1013353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1013348#post1013348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is a question of choice, and I don't want to have to change my religion</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahh. The Lucifuge struck me as a fairly agnostic group with people of many different notions of the supernatural. The only thing they agree upon is that there is a good and evil, and there are beings which seem to represent material evil (demons). They aren't even sure about angels, as they don't seem to represent some objective good.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I don't know how the notion of an omnipotent being of good being in charge of everything would survive exposure to a world with things like the God Machine and Seers. Guess that is why True Faith is such a rare and powerful thing in the OWoD!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:26:58-08:00","id":1013356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WaywardPaladin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1013353#post1013353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ahh. The Lucifuge struck me as a fairly agnostic group with people of many different notions of the supernatural. The only thing they agree upon is that there is a good and evil, and there are beings which seem to represent material evil (demons). They aren't even sure about angels, as they don't seem to represent some objective good.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I don't know how the notion of an omnipotent being of good being in charge of everything would survive exposure to a world with things like the God Machine and Seers. Guess that is why True Faith is such a rare and powerful thing in the OWoD!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lucifer isn't really a big evil figure in Judaism, and Satan is a totally different angel who is more God's Prosecutor than anything actually evil. If a group is talking about the battle between God and Lucifer, it's pretty safe to say they're Christian in my experience","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:36:10-08:00","id":1013358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1013356#post1013356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Lucifer isn't really a big evil figure in Judaism, and Satan is a totally different angel who is more God's Prosecutor than anything actually evil. If a group is talking about the battle between God and Lucifer, it's pretty safe to say they're Christian in my experience</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And there are certainly Lucifuge that fit all the possible interpretations. The Adversary as Loyal Opposition that humanity is meant to oppose to display their Virtue, there is a faction that is trying to redeem Lucifer by correcting the mistakes attributed to him. There is a faction that thinks the whole thing is a put on and the Lucifuge is just trying to manipulate them. <br /> <br /> The world demonstrably does not conform to the expectations of an orthodox interpretation of Christianity, and so how a character reacts to that is where things get interesting. A faction of obviously supernatural descendants but with reality not neatly matching any of their preconceived beliefs leaves room for a family of very different minded people all arguing their own interpretation. And the Lucifuge tolerates this. As long as you're not evil or demon worshiping, the Lucifuge has room for all kinds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:51:42-08:00","id":1013361,"title":"","content":"I understand, and I would definitely work with them, but they would not be my first choice if I had a choice of all the groups in the WoD. Besides, I don't remember it's name, but I'm fairly sure there's a Jewish compact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:58:40-08:00","id":1013362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1013361#post1013361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand, and I would definitely work with them, but they would not be my first choice if I had a choice of all the groups in the WoD. Besides, I don't remember it's name, but I'm fairly sure there's a Jewish compact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me know if you remember, I can't name one off the top of my head but I haven't read through ALL the compacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8762-waywardpaladin","name":"WaywardPaladin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T13:59:32-08:00","id":1013364,"title":"","content":"I think it was from the forums","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T19:56:45-08:00","id":1013551,"title":"","content":"Well, if we're allowed to choose mortal splats too then I'll go with mortal cultist like I did on the last one of these. The more eldritch and forbidden the dark patron, the better I say. This is the Chronicles of Darkness after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now, if I had to stick to the monster gameline splats then I'd definitely chose Changeling. They may have the shittyest transformation process and will be hunted for the rest of their lives by the True Fae and their Huntsmen, but Arcadia and the Hedge are still wondrous places. I'd easily see myself falling into the 1E Autumn Court mentality and philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T20:00:53-08:00","id":1013556,"title":"","content":"Gah!<br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">characters</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T17:28:22-08:00","id":1014061,"title":"","content":"It's a hard choice, but I think I'd probably have the easiest time being a Vampire. Carthian or Unaligned, I can't decide, but definitely Mekhet. It'd be really hard watching my loved ones die... which is why I'm not going to! Nope, me becoming a vampire means that my mom, dad, sister, girlfriend, and girlfriend are all going to have to be Embraced. Things might get a little uncomfortable after a while, but we've all got time to learn how to live with it. Anyway, I've already recieved prior permission from my mom, just in case. Not sure how my dad would feel about it... oh well, I could just ask him a few years in. I'm sure he'd be fine, right? Nothing could go wrong here, definitely not. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> Plus, I'm fortunate enough to live in an area that has multiple dungeons and swinger clubs, which I imagine would make regular feeding much less dangerous, and would also net me a sexy entourage! Again, nothing could possibly go wrong here. It would all work out perfectly. Mm-hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:33:04-08:00","id":1014125,"title":"","content":"Union Home First member, probably getting frustrated by the local old timers constant refusal to actually help the people who need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T15:30:45-08:00","id":1014484,"title":"","content":"This is odd because today I looked in the mirror and thought &quot;Hey, this guy would make a great Vampire character.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yeah, I would probably be a freshly Embraced Mekhet/Daeva by a sire who grew a very temporary passion for me, he/she would quickly realize the mistake they've made and leave me to defend myself.<br /> <br /> I'll join the Ordo Dracul, or maybe the Islamic variation of the Lancea Sanctum, just because the Carthians wouldn't be present where I live...<br /> <br /> For merits, I'd say Striking Looks (if I do say so myself) and Danger Sense (living in a 3rd world environment does have its &quot;benefits&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 12-08-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T16:07:11-08:00","id":1014497,"title":"","content":"So, given I can <i>technically</i> play one without breaking them game hugely- can I be an Exile? You get all the freedom and autonomy of being a demon with the immortality and the not-being-hunted-down-by-a-realty-warping-supercomputer of being an angel! Admittedly, there is the existential nihilism but, like, same.<br /> <br /> If not (aw) then I would either choose changeling or vampire. Changeling, if I have now escaped the oh-god-why bit, has a lot of cool powers, no huge downsides and a fairly safe world (the Gentry are <i>big</i> threats but it doesn't seem like they're <i>common </i>threats). Also I could go to parties with my fetch and it would be the best prank on all the loved ones I left behind. Fairest would be cool!<br /> <br /> Vampires are mostly miserable except, well, immortal. And that is quite possibly enough to rule out murderous subconscious urges and never seeing the sun, at least for me. I would like to be either Ventrue, because I'm already mentally ill and I might as well get mind control out of it, or Mekhet, because I am already hurt by fire and might as well get to read minds out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T16:10:18-08:00","id":1014498,"title":"","content":"Actually, if we're going for &quot;anything's playable if you have a permissive enough GM&quot;, bagsy a Rank 10 Spirit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T16:44:29-08:00","id":1014513,"title":"","content":"Wyrd 10 Cambion. <br /> <br /> Previous answer below. <br /> <br /> A Wyrd 10, Clarity 10 Darkling or Elemental or Fairest Dearheart or Author Changeling with a very much dead or disinterested Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-19-2017, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T17:54:22-08:00","id":1014546,"title":"","content":"Changeling, if only to play out in a game how military conscription is a generally <i>shitty </i>experience that nevertheless teach some lessons in the hard way. I mean, I never even went to the frontlines, but I've seen that seven seaons of a tightly regulared life, an authoritarian atmosphere, limited freedom, forcibly interacting with people that you could have just ignored in the 'outside' society can mess up people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T18:05:47-08:00","id":1014554,"title":"","content":"Now that Hurt Locker's out, I think being an Atariya or a psychic vampire would be nice.<br /> <br /> In the first case, I'm a hugely risk-averse individual, so the main downside (nobody likes a sore winner who keeps winning) isn't really an issue for me. For the latter, it's all the cool of a vampire with none of the Beast or the long-lasting harm; eating just makes everyone feel winded for a few minutes. Yeah, I'm mortal, but really, eternal life would be mind-shreddingly boring after a while; it's really age and running out of time to live that I fear, and once I've done everything I want in life, I have no problem just letting time catch up with me; I don't need my youth any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T02:45:13-08:00","id":1016471,"title":"","content":"Likely be a less violent version of my mekhet vampire currently. Circle with 'cleaner' style of Cruac, maybe with Carthian leanings. Find some awesome friends, chill out and enjoy the afterlife. Immortality and invisibility are strong pulls~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11516-forgelineage","name":"ForgeLineage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T13:24:28-08:00","id":1016708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1014497#post1014497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, given I can <i>technically</i> play one without breaking them game hugely- can I be an Exile? You get all the freedom and autonomy of being a demon with the immortality and the not-being-hunted-down-by-a-realty-warping-supercomputer of being an angel! Admittedly, there is the existential nihilism but, like, same.<br /> <br /> If not (aw) then I would either choose changeling or vampire. Changeling, if I have now escaped the oh-god-why bit, has a lot of cool powers, no huge downsides and a fairly safe world (the Gentry are <i>big</i> threats but it doesn't seem like they're <i>common </i>threats). Also I could go to parties with my fetch and it would be the best prank on all the loved ones I left behind. Fairest would be cool!<br /> <br /> Vampires are mostly miserable except, well, immortal. And that is quite possibly enough to rule out murderous subconscious urges and never seeing the sun, at least for me. I would like to be either Ventrue, because I'm already mentally ill and I might as well get mind control out of it, or Mekhet, because I am already hurt by fire and might as well get to read minds out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exile sounds too good, and since this is the World/Chronicles of Darkness, that's of course a no-no! (Mostly because I never considered that option and don't wanna admit it, though =P )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T20:35:50-08:00","id":1016890,"title":"","content":"Purified, it'll take some time and care to figure out how to harvest essence safely and a little more care to figure out how to pass the ages safely as technology improves but I also become one of the most enduring entities in the game and I'll have all kinds of time as long as I don't attract the wrong attention.<br /> <br /> Question? Do we get normal character creation + (our age - minus 18) XP or are we effectively blank slates with age - 18 XP. This gets much easier with option A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11422-maskedone","name":"MaskedOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:38:15-08:00","id":1017033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaskedOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1016890#post1016890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Purified, it'll take some time and care to figure out how to harvest essence safely and a little more care to figure out how to pass the ages safely as technology improves but I also become one of the most enduring entities in the game and I'll have all kinds of time as long as I don't attract the wrong attention.<br /> <br /> Question? Do we get normal character creation + (our age - minus 18) XP or are we effectively blank slates with age - 18 XP. This gets much easier with option A.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, generally longevity is a strong motivator; who'd have guessed ? =D<br /> <br /> The former option: basic character creation + (Age - 18) xp. I was working on the assumption that someone at the age of 18 (rather 21, but I leaned towards being more generous ^^) was the go-to age/standard, having finished their education/gotten started in their first job, with people who are older having had more chance to develop (Attributes), make connections (Merits) and learn stuff (Skills), while those who are younger with less of those opportunities.<br /> So yeah, option A all the way. What kind of Purified would you be with that? =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T05:08:13-08:00","id":1019720,"title":"","content":"Hoffnung/Staunen Progenitor<br /> <br /> Failing that, Thyrsus Lib... oh.<br /> <br /> Failing that, Werewolf (Ithaeur/Irraka Iron Master/HiD) or Vampire (Gangrel Carthian w/ Dragon leanings)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:27:09-08:00","id":1020044,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eater, Prey, Gatekeeper, with Primeval and Grave Dirt Keys, with Caul and Shroud Manifestations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12771-revanreborn","name":"RevanReborn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T03:14:06-08:00","id":1020814,"title":"","content":"Hmm, the exclusion of mages rules out my first and most preferred choice, so let's see: immortality (or at least strong potential for it), empowerment (in the sense of self-agency and mastery of my environment; mundane power interests me little, even if mind control abilities are just too useful to neglect), potential for self-development, and mystical awareness would be my main selection criteria. Their mortality rules out being a Werewolf or a Sin-Eater, even if I greatly appreciate their power and insights. Changelings and Demons have remarkable abilities and potential for immortality, but I find being eternally on the run too bothersome a lifestyle, if an adequate alternative is available. However I'd likely find the Durance or giving up my old life to a Fetch not that much of a bother, since I'm resistant to pain and abuse and you can always set up a new life and find new friends and romantic partners elsewhere. I'm selfish and callous enough not to mind a predatory lifestyle to survive, especially since I can try and minimize the damage or focus on preying on those I find worthy of victimization.<br /> <br /> So I'd be OK with being a Daeva Vampire with a bloodline that bestows Dominate as its specialty Discipline (perhaps the Toreador but only if I can focus their artistic obsession on something like martial arts or software development), a generalist effort to develop Blood Potency (up to the point feeding restrictions can be effectively managed with Willpower expenditure, Unnatural Affinity, Blood Price, Willful Vitae, and Sanguinary Invigoration) and most physical and mental Disciplines (espeially Celerity, Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare, Protean, Resilience, and Vigor) regardless of Clan specialization, a main membership in the Ordo Dracul (and a serious effort to master the Coils of the Ascendant, the Wyrm, Zirnitra, and Ziva, and develop a few psychic powers), and a secondary investment in the Circle of the Crone and Cruac. The focus of the Coil of the Voivode on enforcing servitude does not appeal so much to me, although its uses to resist the blood bond and bypass feeding restrictions make its pursuit worthwhile. I'd likely take as little involvement as possible in the political games of the Kindred, only bothering to establish the resources strictly necessary to sustain my Requiem, and I'd focus my immortality on exploring the supernatural, becoming a polymath, and pursuing trans-vampirism. I'd settle for a low-Humanity lifestyle until I can master the Coil of Ziva and use Banes to make myself immune to as many breaking points as possible. I'd keep the blush of life active as much as possible (and pretty much all the time once I master the Coil of the Ascendant) unless I'm starved for Vitae.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I'd also be OK with being a Beast (Eshmaki, Anakim, or Ugallu are all interesting choices) with an Hunger for Prey or Punishment and a focus on developing my Lair, mastering almost all Atavisms (only Infestation really freaks me out) regardless of Family specialization, pursuing the Incarnate Inheritance, becoming a polymath, and exploring the supernatural. I'd settle for a low-Satiety lifestyle, at least until I can master the Incarnate Inheritance. I'm not sure of which Lesson(s) I'd care to teach, since several appeal to me. I'm a bit less interested in Nightmares, but they are certainly useful enough I'd strive to develop most of them for practical reasons.<br /> <br /> My third preferred choice would be a Purified, especially if I can develop and combine spirit and psychic powers. For the record, if the Awakened were available as an option, my first choice would be becoming an Obrimos Mage with a Legacy that provides Life or Mind as a Ruling Arcanum, a main membership in the Mysterium or the Adamantine Arrow and secondary involvement in the other Order, and a focus on developing Gnosis, Forces, Life, Mind, Fate, and Prime. Probably Death too but only insofar it gets useful to achieve immortality or protect oneself; I have zero interest in necromancy. I'd settle for a low-Wisdom lifestyle and eagerly pursue becoming a Lich, and eventually an Archmage.<br /> <br /> In the case I change my mind and deem being a Changeling an acceptable option despite the threat of the True Fae, I'd choose becoming some Dual-Kith hybrid of any two of Hunterheart, Earthbone, Fireheart, Gristlegrinder, or Stonebones. I'd develop ties with the Spring Court, the Summer Court, or both. I'd take a generalist approach to Contracts, since several appeal to me. I'd pursue immortality by Goblin Contracts and building up Wyrd just short of the point one is forced to enter Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are Ugh, No, Just No for too many reasons (I do not mind a nomadic lifestyle, but their existence is endless punishment with the only respite being a pontless return to being a puny mortal) and mummies usually look forward to an eternity of being slaves and experiencing an endless cycle of loss. In comparison, the Coils or the Incarnate Inheritance offer a respite from most drawbacks of the vampire or beast condition I'd find meaningful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-19-2017, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T04:05:14-08:00","id":1021218,"title":"","content":"What I wish to be is irrelevant.<br /> I'd probably be a Nidmuzug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/402-clockro4ch","name":"Clockro4ch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T08:08:14-08:00","id":1021278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1013364#post1013364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was from the forums</div> </div> </div> </div>Hakollel Shel Hamerkava is written by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1009125#post1009125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah... Could I be a Princess? Wouldn't necessary be a fan of being called a Princess all the time and would hope that my supernatural clique would come up a gender neutral name, but the Magical Girl superpowers and sweet outfits do appeal to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bBeing a batshit Genius wouldn't be so bad either so as long as I get cool looking goggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Princesses are also known as Princes or the Enlightened.<br /> <br /> Princess would be my second choice after Purified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T18:20:01-08:00","id":1021448,"title":"","content":"My first answer was a Demon (from Demon the Descent). And it is a very rational, intellectual answer, as in, thinking about it both the powers, outlook and even drawbacks would interest me greatly in being a demon.<br /> <br /> but ...<br /> <br /> The more i read Promethean, the more i get the <i>feeling</i> that being a promethean would be ... fun is definitively not the right word but ... interesting might be closer. Yes being a promethean would suck greatly. After all, thats the concept of the game, them wanting to be us and not us wanting to be them. But the more i look into it, the more i'm finding a deep ... philosophical quality to the life and journey of a promethean that resonate well with the kind of person that i am. I'm not sure i would be able to even reach the great dawn. Would i even want to after learning more about humanity? I dont know, but i like these kind of questions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> I don't even know what lineage i would be. Maybe an alternate, ghost-aspected kind-of ulgan or an osirian as i consider myself an academic. Or maybe i would be my own thing. <br /> The point being, i'm not even sure why exactly being a promethean would interest me so, it is more of a feeling than a fully articulate thought. But its there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T18:38:21-08:00","id":1021451,"title":"","content":"You know... thought I have: while this is a fun question and all, a different question would be, &quot;what society would you want to be a part of?&quot; A Werewolf Protectorate? The Mysterium? A Freehold?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T02:54:14-08:00","id":1021505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1021451#post1021451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know... thought I have: while this is a fun question and all, a different question would be, &quot;what society would you want to be a part of?&quot; A Werewolf Protectorate? The Mysterium? A Freehold?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good Question! Definitely food for thought. In that regard, being part of a Brood or Krewe sounds the most intriguing to me, closely followed by the Mysterium or Autum Court. I'd definately not like to be part of the Danse Macabre, so the only Vampire Covenant of interest for me would be the Ordo. What about you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:10:05-08:00","id":1030328,"title":"","content":"Easy. Mage.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I know that is against the rules. I picked a Mage because I would be a Mage and Mages famously overcome 'rules.'<br /> <br /> What, you need a spell or something... fine, watch as I call upon the Supernal Arcane of Logic.<br /> <br /> 1: The title is 'You as a Player Character' so I am a Player Character.<br /> 2: Player Characters require Players or they would be Non-Player Characters. (If Player Character then Player)<br /> 3: I have a Player. (<i>modus ponens </i>of 1 and 2)<br /> 4: Anyone would pick a Mage if the game premise was 'What Splat would you want to be?' (If Player, select Mage)<br /> 5: 'My Player' would be included in the set 'Anyone'. (My Player is Player)<br /> 6: My Player would pick a Mage. (<i>modus ponens</i> of 4 and 5)<br /> 7: If My Player would pick a Mage, then I would be a Mage.<br /> :: I am a Mage. (<i>modus ponens </i>hat-trick of 6 and 7)<br /> <br /> Paradox inducing Objection: But the rules say you can't pick a Mage.<br /> <br /> Paradox containing rebuttal: Yes, but I didn't pick; my player did.<br /> <br /> So as you can see, logically I must be Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T17:20:28-08:00","id":1030336,"title":"","content":"Let me break your chain there. I wouldn't pick a Mage, so 4 is inherently false, and it's deeply false since I am not a unique individual, so there is a significant population of potential players who wouldn't, so everything else falls apart.<br /> <br /> Also, it's shit thing to try and sidestep the rules of the thread. You might get away with listing it as an aside(&quot;I would be x, but if Mage were available, I'd be one.&quot;), but flat out ignoring the basis is kind of dickish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T18:21:18-08:00","id":1030368,"title":"","content":"But you aren't just Anyone, ArcaneArts. You're a somebody. The people with the courage to face the other, more horrific options cannot be labelled 'Anyone.' So, as a rule, 'Anyone' would pick a Mage. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> That said: 'Also, it's shit thing to try and sidestep the rules of the thread.' doesn't sound like you were joking. So, eh... I was. It was just a joke. One joke out of 112 genuine posts. I didn't think it was that bad; I certainly didn't intend offense.<br /> <br /> As compensation, I will pick an answer for real. I pick the Venture. You get kickass mind-control powers, can inspire twisted love, be immortal if cautious, bestow immortality on others, and you share your headspace with a beastly animal that wants victory as much as food. Sure, you are a bit aloof and you have to hurt people to survive but aloof isn't absent (you can still care for people even when you don't care about them) and most likely everyone causes harm to someone, so getting over that just means accepting the responsibility of existence. I get it, Vampires be horrific but it beats the other options. Werewolves are chained by their nature, The Lost are hunted, and Princesses have a noble obligation least they die of disbelief. Yeah, Vampire-Jack has issues but he is his own little existential nothing and there is scope in that. (Plus, I could join the Invictus and live my eternal life like a boss.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:52:22-08:00","id":1032273,"title":"","content":"I'm really not sure,<br /> I mean part of me would love being Deava or Ventrue and although I would be carthian, being a vampire i think though might drive me towards Invinctus instead. big fan of ordo though. being dead and having the beast sucks though<br /> Changeling could be cool but i don't want to live my life on the run, could be beast elemental of fairest.<br /> similar issues with demon, but i would probably be an integrator.<br /> the urge to hunt and the brutality of being a werewolf is not for me, but on the other hand they can be awesome<br /> mage has the least downsides (but rules of the thread) - could be mastigos, moros or obrimos.<br /> purified are pretty cool, but you need to die and well that sucks.<br /> kinda curious about the other splats particularly the ones in changing breeds and skin changers there might be something in there that's more me<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12845,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","user":"ahather","date":". 01-15-2017, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T22:38:46-08:00","id":1033888,"title":"","content":"Well now that we've taken mage out, The forums choices are getting difficult, i like that.<br /> <br /> As for me. I'd honestly wanted to stay human but not out of the loop. Hunters Virgil- Ascended Ones (Knives of Paradise) A diplomatic hunter group that's willing to listen and mediate with Supernaturals and able to use abilities made from elixirs and potions to Hunt with, or if encounters go bad. I'm an Inquisitive person at heart, and i always look at Dealing with problems with discussions first off. That aside, i also enjoy the idea of making potions that can give you super-human abilities, although temporary. <br /> <br /> As for a secondary choice i would be an Encrolled mortal probably dealing with Dawn or Autumn Court Changelings. Best to deal with changelings that are trying to do better or at least more knowledgeable about other supernaturals. Also obtaining Goblin Fruits would be a huge Bonus. Course these two splats could possibly overlap if done right.<br /> <br /> I also keep hearing the idea of immortality coming up often within the choices. No offense, but i find immortality boring if not tedious. Longevity is a different story for me, especially if there's a cause to it. For example if my Dedication to My Hunter Group or Changeling Court has given me a potion or Goblin fruit that adds 50 to 100 years to my life.Or maybe a changeling contract i made. To keep doing my duty, they post--poned my aging til my contract is broken. . Then i'm certainly cool with that. Maybe it's just me, But i believe ,if you want to gain even the semblance of immortality. Earn it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:50:20-08:00","id":1034144,"title":"","content":"I've reflect on my choices, and, to clarify, would like the following in order of preference: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Genius - Staunen Progenitor, focusing on biological Automata;</li> <li>Princess - Seeker of Clubs, going for Learn and Govern Charms, and a dip in two Connect ones implied by Court</li> <li><span style=\"color:#FFF0F5\">Mage - Thyrsus Libertine, going for Transhuman Engineer Legacy and Life spells like Speak with Beasts, Heightened Sences, Transform Life and Shapechange.</span></li> <li>Wolfblood - Shape-shited Tell, pretty neat power with interesting but not too serious downsides.</li> <li>Vampire - Gangrel Carthian with Dragon leanings, going for Animalism 1 and Protean 2 right off the bat.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:58:04-08:00","id":1034150,"title":"","content":"i want to be a fetch, because it would at least explain why everything went so wrong so suddenly. and there would be a better, cooler me who could take over my life","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:59:33-08:00","id":1034151,"title":"","content":"on a less mopey note, anyone think Genius should be off-limits for the same reasons as Mage? or are the downsides significant enough to let it through?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:01:45-08:00","id":1034154,"title":"","content":"I think Genius isn't as well known enough to face the problem of everyone choosing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:42:00-08:00","id":1034217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1034151#post1034151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on a less mopey note, anyone think Genius should be off-limits for the same reasons as Mage? or are the downsides significant enough to let it through?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, never being able to trust your own research again (due to Inspiration worming its way in), needing materials to pull off your crap, or being on a greased slippery slope are relevant. The first is subjective, the second is close to real life, and the third is varying applicable to all splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:57:05-08:00","id":1034226,"title":"","content":"it would be hell for someone who was already or wanted to be a normal scientist, but not really for someone who just wants to be the kind of super-scientist you see in comics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:07:28-08:00","id":1034233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1034151#post1034151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on a less mopey note, anyone think Genius should be off-limits for the same reasons as Mage? or are the downsides significant enough to let it through?</div> </div> </div> </div>The number of people going &quot;I'd be a genius!&quot; is significantly lower than the number of people who go &quot;I'd be a mage!&quot; is in these sorts of threads.<br /> <br /> Now personally, I'd still stipulate that you should mention a non fansplat, but it ain't my thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:03:09-08:00","id":1034270,"title":"","content":"that's too bad, because i'm so gonna be a Noble. A life with a purpose that leaves you drained and emotionally broken might be bad, but any purpose that involves helping people has got to be better than having no purpose or motivation to do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:06:20-08:00","id":1034272,"title":"","content":"You could just be a human-sympathetic werewolf. Hunt the enemies of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:25:42-08:00","id":1034283,"title":"","content":"sure. If we are sticking to canon splats. If not, i'd rather not have to either spend 50% of my time in the terrifying Shadow or whatever I need to do to balance my Harmony and not have Death Rage on a hair trigger","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 01-18-2017, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:27:34-08:00","id":1034284,"title":"","content":"double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T15:58:09-08:00","id":1034302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1034283#post1034283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sure. If we are sticking to canon splats. If not, i'd rather not have to either spend 50% of my time in the terrifying Shadow or whatever I need to do to balance my Harmony and not have Death Rage on a hair trigger</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to spend any time in the Shadow, you could just hunt the enemies of humans. Hunting balances you towards the spirit, though a minute dip every once and awhile would help. Maintaining balance is fairly easy if you're not in a constant-activity lifestyle like a PC might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T21:24:18-08:00","id":1034450,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I didnt think about fan-splats, kinda forgot about them + dont know much about them. Good point though, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T05:51:14-08:00","id":1034539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1034302#post1034302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't have to spend any time in the Shadow, you could just hunt the enemies of humans. Hunting balances you towards the spirit, though a minute dip every once and awhile would help. Maintaining balance is fairly easy if you're not in a constant-activity lifestyle like a PC might have.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Problem is that I want a constant-activity lifestyle if I'm going to be a protector. Otherwise, I have the same feeling adrift problem, just with super-powers and worse anger issues","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T15:46:48-08:00","id":1034906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1014554#post1014554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that Hurt Locker's out, I think being an Atariya or a psychic vampire would be nice.<br /> <br /> In the first case, I'm a hugely risk-averse individual, so the main downside (nobody likes a sore winner who keeps winning) isn't really an issue for me. For the latter, it's all the cool of a vampire with none of the Beast or the long-lasting harm; eating just makes everyone feel winded for a few minutes. Yeah, I'm mortal, but really, eternal life would be mind-shreddingly boring after a while; it's really age and running out of time to live that I fear, and once I've done everything I want in life, I have no problem just letting time catch up with me; I don't need my youth any more.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes for minor Template Psychic Vampire is hard to beat. <br /> <br /> For major template I'd pick Cambions. <br /> <br /> I actually changed my mind about picking Changeling when it dawned on me that 2e Cambions get many of the benefits of Changeling, don't have to go through an abusive stay in Arcadia, and your hard to kill, and huntsmen have no reason to bother you. <br /> <br /> You do lose out on some advantages and it means having a very strange parent, but it's the balanced choice. Downsides are 1 Changeling entitlement that hates you, you can have some unfortunate effects on the dreams of those near you, in that they don't have them. Hedge Warping might be challenging for you. <br /> <br /> And I think if you get your Wyrd up to 10 your immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T21:28:00-08:00","id":1035055,"title":"","content":"Cambions aren't major templates, don't have Wyrd, primarily only have &quot;I see things no one will ever openly admit to believing in&quot; and lucid dreaming as powers, and are highly sought after by the Gentry, which means you'd probably go through all of those downsides of being a changeling you don't want while becoming a changeling.<br /> <br /> Not a great plan, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:35:02-08:00","id":1040315,"title":"","content":"Definitely a Sin-eater. Changeling and Demons have the problem of 'all powerful being trying to capture/kill you,' Mages are too weird for me, Hunters are boring, Werewolf lifestyle has nothing I really want, Vampire would mean I have to change my entire life. Prometheans are sad. Beasts and Mummies are too unhuman.<br /> <br /> But a Sin-eater is just right for me. I get to live a life of magic and a near-lack of consequences. I'm functionally immune to permanent death, alive again, and I get to help ghosts. I don't have to be scared of pretty much anything in the world anymore, because nothing can stop me as long as I'm not an idiot. The only problem is the Geist, but really? I'm flexible, and I always wanted a proper imaginary friend as a child.<br /> <br /> Hell, if it really existed, I would seek it out willingly. Sounds like fun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T20:27:13-08:00","id":1043335,"title":"","content":"If I had to suffer the miserable, horrific fate of being turned into one of these creatures (that removes unchained from the plate since they were never human to begin with), I think Changeling would be ok. There's abuse, torture and running from my durance (assuming I didn't like it and managed to escape) parts, but there's just <i>so much wonder</i> to be seen with fey eyes... It would still be a miserable existence of running, not trusting people and coping, but the upsides could make it less sucky than say, being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:24:19-08:00","id":1045341,"title":"","content":"As for many before, first choice would be Mage (Mystagogue Acanthus) but since that's out of the question:<br /> <br /> Hunter is a template, right?<br /> Ashwood Abbey Hunter. There's no 2E yet, but assuming a same or similar amount of Merit points (plus some for being old):<br /> Resources 5<br /> Status(Ashwood Abbey):1<br /> Bacchanal 5 for getting some longevity goodies in trade from various supernatural contacts I can get through this, and it's rather nicely diverse in utility in general<br /> Atariya: Damn Lucky 5, Mr. Lucky 1, Easy Come, Easy Go 1<br /> <br /> In addition to all other Hunter things from just character creation, the Atariya Merits make for a reckless but less easily killable hunter of the weird. Adding to that obscene amounts of money and massive parties with supernaturals and famous people, and we end up with someone nothing like me. But sounds fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A significant advantage to the more monstrous templates I didn't see mentioned is losing the Integrity mechanic; I see that as a strong removal from humanity, and a very attractive thing - humans get worn down by the various traumatic events in life. Even if it's not the WoD, effective immunity to trauma-based unraveling is excellent on its own.<br /> <br /> So for a more monstrous splat, Ventrue with lots of Dominating and a nice set of humans for blood so each is fed upon only once in a while. Not the best of lives, but could be quite good, and effective immortality is a nice boost <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:16:06-08:00","id":1045707,"title":"","content":"It's a tough question, what splat I'd want to be. Mage might be alright, but I genuinely don't know how I'd cope with all the supernal symbols on top of the normal sensory overload I sometimes have to deal with.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd rather stick to a minor splat, but if I had to go with a major one, I think I'd actually want to be a Beast. They seem to have the fewest downsides, and provided I feed smartly and hang out with some other supernaturals, they have lots of cool powers, and I'd get to explore the weird, supernatural cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T08:41:57-08:00","id":1045787,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11842_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11842\" data-vbnamecard=\"11842\">Aeryes</a> Interesting choice. What about all the debased, unmoralic stuff they Ashwood Abbey does, though? =D Would you see yourself as part of the Competitors, the Pursuit or the Libertines?<br /> <br /> The Integrity thing cuts both ways, though. It is a removal from humanity, in a way. But I can still see why it's appealing/interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T13:18:39-08:00","id":1045944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1045787#post1045787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11842_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11842\" data-vbnamecard=\"11842\">Aeryes</a> Interesting choice. What about all the debased, unmoralic stuff they Ashwood Abbey does, though? =D Would you see yourself as part of the Competitors, the Pursuit or the Libertines?<br /> <br /> The Integrity thing cuts both ways, though. It is a removal from humanity, in a way. But I can still see why it's appealing/interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way does it cut other than away from humanity?<br /> For the human I am now, being unaffected by trauma sound monstrous, but if I were to be a monster (Vamp, Wolfie, Mage, etc) the traumatic things would be much more frequent, and it would unequivocally be a good thing to not be torn by such. My vamp self might sentimentally prattle about woefully being cut off from humanity in this way, but it's definetly good.<br /> <br /> For the Abbeyists, power does corrupt, if anything Mage shows that rather nicely, the Atariya examples too, and the very existence of the Ashwood Abbey as well.<br /> So yes, the new self I crafted there would spiral into depravity and immorality and ultimately death very quickly, so much so that the potential longevity that he might trade from whatever supers he drew into the bacchanaliae would be of little use. Years, if lucky (hey, Atariya, so years). But what a death it would be, likely during the grandest Bacchanal manageable - Libertine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The background logic of it all is that if I'm importing a fantasy, let it be the fantasy of grand pleasure.<br /> <br /> If I were to pretend to be a little wise (if Wise is out of the question :P) I would go with the answer that Michael Swaim gave for his choice of &quot;superpower&quot; in a cracked.com's After Hours episode: &quot;I'd be Batman. Then I'd stop being Batman and just be a rich guy.&quot;<br /> So a Hunter at Tier zero or one, that's a template, ish. Either none or a small number of Hunter friends to take out that one thing we noticed. Maybe finance them later.<br /> Resources 5, because being rich is our world's version of a monstrous superpower one has to stay human in the face of, Allies to help me take out that one thing that got me hunting and then never hunt again.<br /> And I would still load up on Atariya stuff because it's so very convenient: like Mage, the only drawback is the very advantage you get, and your potential failure in dealing with it. Since I'm down 1 in Abbey Status and 5 in Bacchanal (the more grounded me doesn't really do social butterfly things anyway :P) I can go more fully into the lucky thing, and grab some stuff to actually use on society without being too conspicuous: See The Flow 5 makes me choose who does well and who fails miserably, in many situations. Governments would rise and fall on my judgement's call.<br /> <br /> This version has many pitfalls as well. Likely a longer and more fullfilled life than the Ashwood guy in my previous incarnation, but let's face it, the Atariya go down hard too. Likely mowed down by a dozen gangsters or somesuch after I get exceedingly careless and sky high on the feeling of invincibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T19:16:56-08:00","id":1046123,"title":"","content":"Probably Changeling. I like the wordplay, the manipulating fate, the trickery, along with the fantastical and strange elements. Where else can you get a tuxedo sewn from darkness that not only lets you fit in at the latest gala but also lets you turn invisible for a while? But then again, that's why my Changeling's in Spring: Focus on all the good stuff and try to put the bad behind you. Don't ignore it happened, but don't let it control you and enjoy life as best you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5413-icefyer","name":"Icefyer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T17:28:15-08:00","id":1054101,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's a bit hard to choose, but I think I might choose either a Beast (Anakim or Eshmaki), or a Changeling (Darkling). If fan games are allowed, then I would definitely choose to be a Leviathan, it would be so awesome to basically be a sea god.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T04:44:12-08:00","id":1059436,"title":"","content":"Does Dude of Legend count as a template? If so, one of those.<br /> <br /> If not... probably a Genius. A Hoffnung Progenitor with Exelixi and Epikrato. Or a Neid Artificer with Automata and Prostasia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:25:55-08:00","id":1059626,"title":"","content":"Shoot, no Mages... Is a Sleepwalker Acolyte to a Mage acceptable? I just really love wizards, man.<br /> <br /> All the other CofD splats kind of <i>suck</i> to be - that's part of the point. Every single one of them has to give up something of who they were in order to be who they are. Not that Mages don't, but Mages are also wizards, and it's pretty awesome to be a wizard. I feel like a mortal alchemist (from Promethean) is kind of cheating.<br /> <br /> I guess being a Sin-Eater would be pretty cool (I'm pretty indifferent to Geist but you have to admit that they get a pretty good deal in comparison to the others.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:45:47-08:00","id":1059687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1059626#post1059626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shoot, no Mages... Is a Sleepwalker Acolyte to a Mage acceptable? I just really love wizards, man.<br /> <br /> All the other CofD splats kind of <i>suck</i> to be - that's part of the point. Every single one of them has to give up something of who they were in order to be who they are. Not that Mages don't, but Mages are also wizards, and it's pretty awesome to be a wizard. I feel like a mortal alchemist (from Promethean) is kind of cheating.<br /> <br /> I guess being a Sin-Eater would be pretty cool (I'm pretty indifferent to Geist but you have to admit that they get a pretty good deal in comparison to the others.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, being a Beast is a pretty sweet deal, all things considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:03:36-08:00","id":1059699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1059687#post1059687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, being a Beast is a pretty sweet deal, all things considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read <i>Beast</i>, so I can't say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:13:54-08:00","id":1059705,"title":"","content":"I know mages are awesome, that's why I cut them out =P<br /> <br /> An alchemist would be fine, though Sin-Eater really is cool. Didn't care for it before I read it. It has a certain appeal, and while not my first choice to play (those would be Beast and Promethean), I love it dearly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:05:54-08:00","id":1059736,"title":"","content":"Now, I should add an addendum - the question was &quot;which splat would you <i>want </i>to be&quot; and Sin-Eater is the one I'd <i>choose </i>but it's worth pointing out that no splat in any game ever has ever felt more like 'me' than the Cahalith Werewolf.<br /> <br /> I'm not even a big fan of Werewolf. They're just pretty much me. (and, I imagine, a lot of us STs.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:31:11-08:00","id":1059821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994648-you-as-a-player-character-what-splat-would-you-want-to-be?p=1059736#post1059736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I should add an addendum - the question was &quot;which splat would you <i>want </i>to be&quot; and Sin-Eater is the one I'd <i>choose </i>but it's worth pointing out that no splat in any game ever has ever felt more like 'me' than the Cahalith Werewolf.<br /> <br /> I'm not even a big fan of Werewolf. They're just pretty much me. (and, I imagine, a lot of us STs.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't suit me (if I were describe myself with a splat, I'd probably go with Obrimos Mage), but then, I'm mostly ST/DM because nobody else seems to want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T00:24:40-08:00","id":1059975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container 